-- title:
--   Content of a principal idèle is the principal fractional ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field and let $\alpha \in K^\times$ be a unit of $K$. Form the idèle attached to $\alpha$ by applying `Units.map` to the structure map $K \to \mathbb{A}_K$ (the adèle ring `AdeleRing (𝓞 K) K`), and let `projFin` send it to the finite idèle group $(\mathbb{A}_{K,\mathrm{fin}})^\times$, i.e. take its second component under the identification of the units of a product with the product of the unit groups of the infinite and finite adèle rings. Apply to this finite idèle the homomorphism `fadContentHom`, which sends a finite idèle $u$ to the finitary product $\prod_{v} (\text{primeUnit}\,v)^{\mathrm{placeOrd}(u,v)}$ over the height-one primes $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$, where $\text{primeUnit}\,v$ is the invertible fractional ideal determined by the prime ideal $v$ and $\mathrm{placeOrd}(u,v) = -\log$ of the $v$-adic valuation of the $v$-component of $u$. The assertion is that the fractional ideal of $\mathcal{O}_K$ underlying the resulting unit of $(\mathrm{FractionalIdeal}\ (\mathcal{O}_K)^{0}\ K)^\times$ equals $\mathrm{spanSingleton}\,(\alpha)$, the principal fractional ideal generated by $\alpha$.
--
--   This is the statement that the content (ideal) map on idèles carries a principal idèle to the principal fractional ideal it generates, one half of the dictionary between idèle classes and ray classes. It is used in the construction of Hecke characters of finite order from ray-class data, in particular in the results relating the ray symbol to values at uniformizer idèles and to archimedean local characters.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HeckeCharacter_coe_fadContentHom_projFin_unitsMap_algebraMap.lean

